Package: telltale
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: telltale developers <https://github.com/donaldsteele/telltale/issues>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/donaldsteele/telltale
Description: backdoor and tamper detector for Linux machines (server)
 telltale tells whether a Linux machine has been backdoored. It compares the
 machine with a known-good snapshot, checks system files against the
 distribution's signed packages, runs a hardening checklist and looks for
 things that are suspicious on any machine. It reports and never fixes:
 every finding comes with the command that would fix it.
 .
 This package holds the full telltale binary (/usr/bin/telltale), whose
 server keeps the snapshots and visits enrolled machines over SSH on a
 schedule, and the collector binaries it copies to them on each visit
 (/usr/lib/telltale, for amd64 and arm64). The service is not started on
 installation; see /usr/share/doc/telltale/README.md.
